WEBVTT

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.870
Duel clear.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:21.360
Unlocking.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:30.800
Cleaning.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.780
Cleaning.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.560
Cleaning.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.010
Hurry up!

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.910
I’m home.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:58.580
Oh oh!

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.260
What?

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:27.920
Damn!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:48.830
We’re accepting entries for the World Duel Carnival!

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.900
It was bad.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.300
I couldn’t kattobing during today’s test.

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.120
Have you <i>ever</i> managed
to kattobing during a test?

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.460
I’m always kattobing!

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.930
What’s wrong?

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:07.310
Did it get separated from its mother?

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.380
An obot?

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.840
Why is it there?

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:18.850
Is it broken?

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.440
It looks like they’re saying something.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.500
What?

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.250
They wanted to save their mother.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.910
Thank goodness.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:40.430
Hey, Yuma.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:43.540
Can we also save this obot?

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:45.640
Don’t be crazy.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.190
This is that, so...

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.640
This cord is...

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.050
Yuma, you know what to do?

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.100
Not at all.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.570
Yuma, try connecting the cord in the back.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.040
I should connect this?

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:12.170
Try using this.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.340
I’ll try.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:30.240
Garbage.

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:34.280
Since it’s trying to throw away the trash, it’s fixed.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.070
I’m not garbage!

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.780
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.910
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.830
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.090
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:03.470
In truth, I was sad until I met you

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:09.990
I lied, thinking it was easier to be alone

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:16.560
Even though we don’t like the same books or hobbies

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.440
You’re the only one who agreed with me

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.570
Joy and sadness and anger and do re mi fa so la ti do

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:25.420
There’s no harmony and scenario without differences

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:28.740
Everyone is not the same

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:33.660
That’s the reason for living

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:38.920
Even if the sounds are dissonant at times

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:44.340
That’s why I never give up
I believe my strength will get me through

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.600
I travel to the edge of the world

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:52.060
The sights I see with you are the truth

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.890
Whether it’s rain, wind, blizzard or the scorching sun

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.150
They give color to each day
Will and love keep me from losing heart

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.530
Your kindness was harsh
I learned frustration when we clashed

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:05.200
Freedom begins by accepting differences Dance and create the universe

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:11.830
You...

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.920
\hYuma vs Cleaning Robot Obomi\h

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:17.920
Number 21:

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.970
Sheesh, it followed us.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.550
Sheesh.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.010
In that case, why don’t you look after it, Yuma?

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:28.220
You’ve gotta be kidding!

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:31.190
I’m too busy dueling!

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.440
Duel!

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.520
What?

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:43.770
You can duel?

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.810
But you don’t have a deck.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.160
Duel!

00:06:04.710 --> 00:06:08.430
I activate the spell card Star Light, Star Bright.

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:17.230
When my monsters have the same number of ATK or DEF, their Levels become the same as one of the monsters.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:24.390
Junk Robot Teapot Kangaroo will become the same Level 4 as Junk Robot Camelcycle.

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:28.990
I overlay Level 4 Teapot Kangaroo and Camelcycle.

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:34.380
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.190
Xyz Summon.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.950
Appear, Wind-Up Zenmaister!

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.710
Zenmaister attacks Yuma directly.

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:56.380
You’re an incredible obot!

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.480
You suck.

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.310
What?

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:04.230
Yuma, this machine is clearly better
at dueling than you.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.440
You’re incredible!

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.720
What?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:18.130
Spinning...

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:20.520
But it seems happy.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:24.280
Is this obot a girl?

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.760
This obot?

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.990
It’s not fair to call her an obot.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:31.300
Let’s give her a cute name.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:33.020
Obo...

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.300
How about Obomina Shining Romanoff?

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:36.980
What kind of name is that?

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:37.720
What’s wrong with it!

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:40.620
Obomi is fine.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.230
Obomi!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.020
Obomi!

00:07:47.140 --> 00:07:49.770
She seems to like you, Yuma.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:52.070
Yuma.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:56.240
My hands are already full
since Astral is staying with me!

00:07:56.670 --> 00:08:01.160
Obomi stay.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.580
Good night, Obomi.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:34.610
Preparations are complete.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:40.380
Obots, you’ll do plenty of cleaning again.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:10.540
Obomi!

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.970
Where did she go?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:20.910
What?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:23.720
Is this supposed to be a goodbye note?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.090
I’m home.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:31.110
Another jewel robbery?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:37.090
I promise to get the scoop!

00:09:37.090 --> 00:09:41.080
Yuma, help me.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.560
Why all of a sudden?

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:45.720
Jewel robbery?

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:51.280
I secretly acquired and analyzed
the security camera footage.

00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:54.280
But it’s not enough to learn anything.

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:00.700
That’s...

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.290
Can it be?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.620
Obomi?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:09.960
The thief is a genius duelist.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:14.340
He can easily open safes with super difficult duel tests.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:16.310
I see.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:21.260
Obomi has the dueling tactical
skills to be the thief.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.310
It’s Obomi?

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:27.480
Once the crime starts, the police arrive on the scene approximately 17 minutes later.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:31.160
The thief must vanish by then.

00:10:31.160 --> 00:10:32.480
That means...

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.490
Let’s determine the area up to
17 minutes away from each crime scene.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:42.410
The criminal’s hideout is the location where they merge.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.200
I see!

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.410
Wait, Yuma!

00:10:56.900 --> 00:11:00.090
I made a lot of money again tonight.

00:11:00.520 --> 00:11:04.650
No one knows that I’m using
obots to steal jewels—

00:11:04.650 --> 00:11:06.140
Whatever!

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.270
Who are you?

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:13.840
Be quiet!

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.530
How dare you force Obomi to commit crimes?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.410
Obomi?

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.030
What are you talking about?

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:23.530
That’s my faithful servant!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.430
You’re wrong! Obomi is our friend!

00:11:26.430 --> 00:11:29.150
Now give back Obomi!

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.290
Take care of them!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.340
Hey, Obomi!

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.260
Don’t you remember us?

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.220
Obomi...

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.930
Obomi?

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:50.640
Obomi!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:54.450
Obomi doesn’t remember us!

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:55.690
Yuma...

00:11:56.360 --> 00:11:59.220
Obomi, let’s duel!

00:11:59.220 --> 00:12:00.280
Duel...

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.600
Duel target confirmed.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:03.990
I will defeat him in a duel.

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:07.560
Yuma, do you have a strategy in mind?

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:11.540
No, but maybe this card will help.

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:18.050
Obomi, I’ll make you remember us by dueling!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:22.270
AR Vision Link complete.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:23.430
Duel!

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.050
Yuma...

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.140
I’ll go first!

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.850
My turn! I draw!

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:32.100
I summon Gagaga Magician!

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.280
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:42.280
My turn. I draw.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:46.280
I activate Eco Spell - Reduce Waste.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:53.660
I banish two Junk Robot monsters in my deck to add Junk Robot Camelcycle to my hand.

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:57.540
I summon Camelcycle.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:02.580
Then I activate Eco Spell - Recycle.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:08.140
I can Special Summon up to two banished Junk Robot monsters.

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:15.810
I Special Summon Junk Robot Cleanaga and Junk Robot Computerkong.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:16.810
Is it coming?

00:13:17.340 --> 00:13:21.280
I overlay three Level 4 Junk Robots.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:25.200
With these three monsters, I build the Overlay Network.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.780
Xyz Summon.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:30.460
Appear, Recycle Rhinobot.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:37.710
Rhinobot attacks Gagaga Magician!

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:38.860
Yuma!

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:39.420
I know!

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:43.130
I activate the trap Half Unbreak!

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:48.300
One monster on my field isn’t destroyed, and I only take half the damage!

00:13:55.090 --> 00:13:59.060
Has Obomi really forgotten about us?

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.820
I’ll make you remember, Obomi!

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:05.280
My turn! I draw!

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:08.740
I summon a new friend!

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:11.530
Come, Gagaga Girl!

00:14:21.050 --> 00:14:23.250
My Gagaga elder!

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:30.180
I equip the Equip Spell Wonder Wand on Gagaga Girl!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:35.560
The Spellcaster-Type monster gains 500 ATK!

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:36.770
Good.

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.360
You now have the formula for victory.

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:42.060
I activate Gagaga Magician’s effect!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:47.070
Gagaga Magician’s Level changes from 4 to 8 until the End Phase!

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:50.050
Why, Yuma?

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:53.590
Then I activate the spell card Gagaga Thunder!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:15:03.170
I select two Gagaga monsters, and you take damage equal to the difference in their Levels multiplied by 300 points!

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:07.380
The Level difference between Level 8 Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Girl is 5!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:11.050
Therefore, you take 1500 points of damage!

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:18.270
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:22.980
Gagaga Magician’s Level changes back from 8 to 4 at the End Phase!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:25.270
Yuma, why?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.950
Gagaga Girl’s effect can make the opponent’s Xyz Monster have 0 ATK.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:37.700
You could’ve changed Gagaga Magician’s Level to be the same as Gagaga Girl’s Level 3 and Xyz Summon Leviathan Dragon.

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:43.170
If it attacked Rhinobot with 0 ATK, you would’ve won.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.310
Winning isn’t enough!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:48.880
Obomi!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.410
My turn.

00:15:50.850 --> 00:15:51.880
I draw.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:55.180
I summon Junk Robot Teapot Kangaroo.

00:15:57.810 --> 00:16:00.480
Rhinobot’s effect activates.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:07.190
By using one Overlay Unit, my other monsters gain 500 ATK.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.650
This is bad!

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:15.160
I use three Overlay Units, so Teapot Kangaroo gains 1500 ATK.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:17.870
2300 ATK?

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:21.330
First, Rhinobot attacks Gagaga Girl.

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:26.180
I flip over the trap card Gagagaguard!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:33.090
When there are two or more Gagaga monsters, Gagaga can’t be destroyed in battle this turn!

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:40.150
Teapot Kangaroo attacks Gagaga Magician.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:43.520
Gagagaguard, protect Gagaga Magician too!

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.150
Yuma!

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:58.580
Yuma, what are you thinking?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:04.040
I’m going to have that same duel again.

00:17:04.720 --> 00:17:05.870
Do you mean...

00:17:06.340 --> 00:17:10.210
You’re recreating your duel against Obomi?

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.830
Come back, Obomi.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:18.620
Let’s have a fun duel again!

00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:21.060
Obomi!

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.730
Come back, Obomi!

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.730
Rhinobot’s... effect... activates...

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:40.010
When my monster doesn’t have any Overlay Units, the monster with the fewest ATK is destroyed during the End Phase.

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:46.790
Both players take damage equal to the destroyed monster’s original ATK.

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:55.130
Yuma, if this effect activates again next turn, you and Obomi will both have 0 LP.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:58.800
I won’t let this duel end until I draw that card!

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:04.770
It’s almost time for the device to activate.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.440
What?

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.650
Bomb program is active.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:19.980
In one minute, the program will be impossible to stop.

00:18:20.950 --> 00:18:23.000
What do you mean?

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.870
Obomi is going to explode?

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:31.010
To prevent that, Obomi herself must stop the program within a minute.

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.090
One minute...

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:36.090
Yuma, everything depends on your next draw.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:38.550
My draw...

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:48.980
I’m kattobing! I draw!

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:51.440
Here it is!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:57.150
I activate the spell card Star Light, Star Bright from my hand!

00:18:58.490 --> 00:19:06.520
When I have at least two monsters with the same attack or DEF, their Levels become the same as one of the monsters!

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:12.180
I make Gagaga Girl’s Level equal Gagaga Magician’s! She’s now Level 4!

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:24.260
You... suck...

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.680
That’s right, Obomi! Come back to us!

00:19:26.680 --> 00:19:28.120
Obomi?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.070
I see!

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:33.690
Yuma is recreating his duel against Obomi to make her remember us!

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:42.610
You suck.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.620
Hooray! Obomi!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.710
Obomi!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:58.390
Obomi isn’t free yet?

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.800
Then I’ll go a step further!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:05.790
I overlay Level 4 Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Girl!

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:11.140
With these two monsters,
I build the Overlay Network!

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:13.480
Xyz Summon!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:19.820
Appear, Number 39: Utopia!

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.010
Yuma!

00:20:25.010 --> 00:20:25.910
Obomi!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.910
I activate Gagaga Girl’s effect!

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:37.630
When Gagaga Girl and Gagaga Magician both become Overlay Units, one of your Xyz Monsters’s ATK becomes 0!

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:42.010
I make Rhinobot have 0 ATK!

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:44.720
Obomi, I’ll rescue you now!

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.640
Hope Sword Slash!

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.780
Obomi!

00:21:12.520 --> 00:21:15.710
Yuma, you suck...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:20.880
Hooray!

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:23.330
That stupid junk robot!

00:21:23.330 --> 00:21:24.640
It’s fine.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:28.550
I brought a spare bomb.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:29.470
I brought one.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:30.510
I brought one.

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:33.020
You fools!

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.810
The criminal in the serial jewel robbery case was arrested last night.

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:45.610
How frustrating!

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:49.120
I was supposed to get the scoop!

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.380
I’m leaving!

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:54.800
Yuma, duel food.

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:55.920
Whoa!

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:58.330
With this, my dueling will be perfect today!

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:01.040
Yuma, you suck.

00:22:02.850 --> 00:22:04.010
Hey!

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:08.880
Stop that! I don’t suck!

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:16.040
Let’s start the duel!

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:18.640
This week’s quiz:

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:24.540
What’s the name of the summoning method that uses two or more monsters with the same Level?

00:22:30.070 --> 00:22:34.830
Today’s test is hard
Can’t avoid pleasure and temptation

00:22:34.830 --> 00:22:39.920
I want to go home and watch TV
Recent cartoons are entertaining

00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:54.430
Anyway, tests are hard
Language, math and English are especially hard

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:59.520
Average scores in science and social studies
I’m only good at P.E.

00:22:59.520 --> 00:23:01.940
(Wait, Baby!) The expected

00:23:01.940 --> 00:23:04.570
(What’s that, Baby!) Answers

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:07.290
(Wait a sec, Baby!) Remember them

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:08.860
(What are we!? Baby!) For who

00:23:08.860 --> 00:23:13.590
Let’s say I wrote the correct answers on that sheet

00:23:13.590 --> 00:23:18.080
Will that change the future a year or a decade from now?

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:23.530
The world I drew at the edge of dreams

00:23:23.530 --> 00:23:28.130
Someday I’ll race in the sky

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:33.260
Nobody can threaten my heart

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:37.100
Nothing is correct!

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:45.560
Kaito the Number Hunter
finally appeared at my school!

00:23:45.560 --> 00:23:47.690
Who did this?

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:49.820
The King’s Key is missing!

00:23:50.280 --> 00:23:52.320
Someone stole my key?

00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:54.570
Astral is inside it!

00:23:54.570 --> 00:23:55.940
Yuma!

00:23:55.940 --> 00:23:58.900
Why are Shark and Kaito dueling?

00:23:58.900 --> 00:24:00.680
The power of Zexal...

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:09.920
\h\hThe King’s Key is Stolen! Clash: Kaito vs Shark\h\h

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:06.290
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZEXAL:
“The King’s Key is Stolen! Clash: Kaito vs Shark”

00:24:06.900 --> 00:24:09.200
I’m kattobing!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:14.440
The answer is... Xyz Summon!

00:24:14.440 --> 00:24:20.440
You need to gather monsters with the same Level on the field to Xyz Summon.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:24.940
You should Xyz Summon and call out powerful monsters!
